Can you explain to me in simple terms what the C++ "r"-term means? 
 assistant
The "r"-term in C++ is a way to specify the direction of execution of a conditional statement. It is used to specify whether the statement will be executed if a condition is true or false.

For example, if a conditional statement is written like this:

if (condition) {
  // code if condition is true
} else {
  // code if condition is false
